  "notes": "Originally a military term meaning to assemble troops, now commonly used in civilian contexts for gathering people for events, projects, or emergencies. Also used for box office/attendance figures.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {動員|どういん}する (to mobilize)\n- {動員|どういん}される (to be mobilized)\n- {動員|どういん}をかける (to call for mobilization)\n- {観客|かんきゃく}{動員|どういん}{数|すう} (audience attendance numbers)\n- {総|そう}{動員|どういん} (total mobilization)",
